
How to debug gprofng-gui with the netbeans IDE.


------ how to create JAVA IDE project from scratch -------

1. create a workspace
  hg clone git://ca-tools4.us.oracle.com/gprofng-gui.git gprofng-gui.git
  cd gprofng-gui.git

2. build workspace
  mkdir ../dist_gprofng-gui
  ( cd ../dist_gprofng-gui && ../gprofng-gui.git/configure --prefix=`pwd`/INSTALL )
  ( cd ../dist_gprofng-gui && make -j 20 && make install )

3. save workspace dir in copy buffer to paste later
   WORKAREA=`pwd`/gprofng-gui.git

4. launch netbeans and set SP_ANALYZER_ER_PRINT:
  cd gprofng-gui.git
  WORKAREA=`pwd`/gprofng-gui.git  # save workspace dir in copy buffer to paste later
  JDK_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/java; export JDK_HOME
  PATH="${JDK_HOME}/bin:${PATH}" ; export PATH
  SP_ANALYZER_ER_PRINT=%INSTALL_DIR_OF_GPROFNG%/bin/gp-display-text ; export SP_ANALYZER_ER_PRINT

  UDIR=`pwd`/../USER_DIR/NB_user_dir
  mkdir -p "${UDIR}"
  GP_DISPLAY_TEXT=<INSTALL_DIR_OF_GPROFNG>/bin/gp-display-text
  SP_ANALYZER_ER_PRINT=${GP_DISPLAY_TEXT} ; export SP_ANALYZER_ER_PRINT
  /opt/netbeans-12.5/netbeans/bin/netbeans --fontsize 18 --jdkhome ${JDK_HOME} --userdir ${UDIR} &
  
5. Create a new IDE project -----
  Menu: File->New Project
  Choose Project
  Categories  -> Java
  Projects    -> "Java Project with Existing Sources"
  [Next]

  Name and Location <defaults are OK, but if you want a local project:>
  Project Name     -> javaProject
  Project Location -> %WORKAREA%/projects/gprofng-gui.nb
  [Next]

  Existing Sources
  Add Folder       -> %WORKAREA%/com
  [Finish]

6. Set Project Properties ----
  Projects(tab) -> right click on project  -> Properties ->
    Categories -> Libraries -> Compile -> Add JAR/Folder
      %WORKAREA%/import/jh-2.0_05.jar
  [open]
  [ok]

  Projects(tab) -> right click on project  -> Properties ->
    Categories -> Build -> Packaging:
      "Build JAR after Compiling"  -> ON
      "Copy Dependent Libraries"   -> OFF
  [ok]

  Projects(tab) -> right click on project  -> Properties ->
    Categories -> Run
      Main Class        -> org.gprofng.analyzer.AnMain
      Arguments         -> test.1.er (example)
      Working Directory -> <your_test_dir or empty>
  [ok]

